of Men's Health.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:33.567
-Yeah. It's strange, because,
normally, you're doing a movie

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.334
and they ask you to do
a magazine cover

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:37.400
and here we are, Men's Health.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.667
But, this time,
they did both of us,

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.200
both actors from the movie.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.267
-Were you worried that it'd be

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.767
similar photographs?
-Similar. A little.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.901
I mean, a little bit because,
you know,

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:48.901
I don't know if you've seen
Men's Health.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:50.033
They sometimes will --

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.767
they'll kind of have
a similar setup

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:54.934
but I'm like, "Ah,
is this going to be too alike?"

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.501
-Right, right, right.
I actually have --

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:57.901
I have his cover as well

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.067
-Right.
-Of Men's Health.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:00.267
[ Laughter ]
If you want to just take a --

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.334
We'll look at both.
-Well, you'll see --

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.400
you'll get what I'm saying.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.100
I think that like there's a --
-Here's his cover right here.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:05.901
[ Laughter and applause ]
-It's a real --

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:07.801
[ The Roots playing funky jazz ]

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:11.100
[ Cheering ]

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.300
-Yeah.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.767
So -- So, they were like --
they assured me.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.834
They'll say, "Don't worry.
It's not going to be the same,"

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.868
and I see he's by a pool,
so, I was like, "Oh, okay."

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:21.868
[ Laughter ]
-They're different.
-They're different.

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.400
I'm against a wall --
-They're different enough.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.300
-I'm against a wall.
He's at a pool, yeah.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.100
-I went further,
if you don't mind.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.234
I actually looked inside the
magazine at the photo shoots

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:31.133
and see how similar
your shoots are.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.033
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, right.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:33.467
-Like they have casual shots

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:35.133
of you, alright, in the mag.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.701
Here's a casual shot
of Jonathan.

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:37.701
-So, there's Jonathan.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.400
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Hey, now.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.067
-There's
Jonathan's casual shot.
-Dude chilling out.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.300
He probably didn't even know
the camera was there.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.434
-Yeah. Yeah, I know.
It's like he's just hanging out

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:47.901
-By the pool.
-by the pool, again,

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.167
and I'm like, "Well,
what about my casual shot?"

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.367
-Yeah, and here's your --
this is your casual shot.

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:52.434
"Stay with the wall."

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:53.601
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.167
-That's very similar
to the cover.

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.467
-It's kind of --

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.734
-Similar.
-It's similar.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:03.033
It's similar, but this one,
you can see, it's like --

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.767
"Oh, what --
Oh, hey!"

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.300
[ Laughter and applause ]
-You recognize.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.701
At first,
you didn't know who they were.

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.501
-It's like, "Wait, hold on,
you're shooting a picture, what?

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:10.634
Oh, you guys!"

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:11.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.033
-But then there's a --
then there's a --

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.501
there's a thing in Jonathan's

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.400
where they go
through his morning routine.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.934
-Yeah, that's another thing
they like to do.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.501
They want to, you know,
just make you appear

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:21.734
as you normally are,
just, you know,

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:24.000
you get ready for the day or --
-Getting up.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.267
-Yeah, and here's --
so, here's Jonathan with his --

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:27.534
he's having a protein shake.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:30.601
[ Laughter and applause ]
And --

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:33.133
Then, here --
-So, he's drinking his -- yeah.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.434
-Yeah, he's drinking
his protein.

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.801
And here's you
with a glass of juice.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:42.100
[ Cheering ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.634
-Yeah, so --
so, it's kind of the same.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.000
They were like, "Do you want --
What do you want,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.901
