It's "Ant-Man,"

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:15.467
"Ant-Man and the Wasp:
Quantumania."

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:17.367
[ Cheering and applause ]
I saw it.

00:07:17.367 --> 00:07:18.901
It is fantastic.
It is giant.

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:20.701
-Thank you, yeah.
-It's massive.

00:07:20.701 --> 00:07:23.400
I mean, is it --
I don't know.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:27.200
Is it tough to be involved
in a set that's all CGI?

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.000
-There were some days there was
the thing called volume.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.968
And some days we would film
and people said,

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:33.267
[ Whispering ]
"You know, we're going to film
the volume."

00:07:33.267 --> 00:07:36.501
And the volume is
a new technology.

00:07:36.501 --> 00:07:37.934
You know, normally you're
shooting with bluescreens

00:07:37.934 --> 00:07:40.033
all around you,
but it's this --

00:07:40.033 --> 00:07:41.801
it's like an LED screen
that wraps

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.767
around an entire sound stage.

00:07:43.767 --> 00:07:48.000
And so they try and make it feel
as much like the quantum realm

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.834
or whatever and we have
something to react to.

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:52.801
And it was crazy
to go into these sound stages

00:07:52.801 --> 00:07:56.100
and it looked like you were
in outer space, something wild.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.701
-And what is the ground like?
Is it the ground --

00:07:57.701 --> 00:07:59.634
-They put on dirt.
They like have dirt

00:07:59.634 --> 00:08:01.501
and they try and have as much

00:08:01.501 --> 00:08:02.567
practical stuff as possible.
-So you really feel like you're

00:08:02.567 --> 00:08:03.701
on a planet or whatever.

00:08:03.701 --> 00:08:05.434
-You really feel like you're
on a planet

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:07.801
or you're in some weird space.

00:08:07.801 --> 00:08:09.267
One of the things that --
Actually, we went in

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:11.367
and there was dirt all
over the floor

00:08:11.367 --> 00:08:15.901
and we were shooting with like
150 other creatures and people

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:19.200
and it doesn't smell good
at all.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.267
[ Laughter ]
"Mm."

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:22.367
And then throughout the day,

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:23.567
it was kind of getting worse
and worse.

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:25.801
The next day,
it was like overbearing

00:08:25.801 --> 00:08:28.601
and we realized they probably
got a deal on the dirt

00:08:28.601 --> 00:08:31.000
because it actually wasn't dirt.
It was manure.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.367
[ Ohhs and laughter ]

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:33.501
-What?!

00:08:33.501 --> 00:08:35.067
Are you kidding me?
-No.

00:08:35.067 --> 00:08:36.934
-Wow!
-They actually had to kind of

00:08:36.934 --> 00:08:39.601
shut it down for a day
and then bring in some new dirt.

00:08:39.601 --> 00:08:42.567
I don't think anyone knew
and it was --

00:08:42.567 --> 00:08:45.601
-You'd think manure would be
more expensive than dirt.

00:08:45.601 --> 00:08:46.868
-Apparently not.
-Apparently not!

00:08:46.868 --> 00:08:49.667
-Yeah. Yeah. Yeah,
the quantum realm just reeks.

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:52.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Wow! I did not know that.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.200
-Paul, how do we set up
this film?

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.834
I would say it's just
action adventure comedy.

00:08:57.834 --> 00:08:59.767
It's family-friendly.
-Yeah.

00:08:59.767 --> 00:09:01.033
-A lot of family.

00:09:01.033 --> 00:09:03.868
It's a little bit like --
You know, family was,

00:09:03.868 --> 00:09:06.767
I think, a theme in the other
"Ant-Man" movies, and comedy,

00:09:06.767 --> 00:09:08.901
and I think some of that exists
in this one, too,

00:09:08.901 --> 00:09:11.834
but it's
on a much grander scale.

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:15.133
It's starting off Phase 5
of Marvel, which --

00:09:15.133 --> 00:09:15.968
-Whoa!

00:09:15.968 --> 00:09:19.067
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:09:19.067 --> 00:09:21.801
-Which is very exciting,
introducing a new

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:24.467
big, bad villain called
Kang the Conqueror.

00:09:24.467 --> 00:09:27.400
-Yeah.
-Which is, if you look
at those pictures of Jonathan,

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.467
I think you could probably
buy him as a conqueror.

00:09:29.467 --> 00:09:30.801
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, that's Kang.

00:09:30.801 --> 00:09:32.601
-He's fantastic.
-He really is.

00:09:32.601 --> 00:09:34.367
-And so, yeah --
-Everyone's great.

00:09:34.367 --> 00:09:36.501
-It just feels like a much --
-Michelle Pfeiffer is fantastic.

00:09:36.501 --> 00:09:38.534
[ Cheering ]
-She's always great.
-Evangeline Lilly.

00:09:38.534 --> 00:09:40.033
-Great.
-Bill Murray.

00:09:40.033 --> 00:09:41.367
-How about that?
-Yeah.

00:09:41.367 --> 00:09:43.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah. Awesome.
-Come on.

00:09:43.267 --> 00:09:45.567
And you! And you got you.
-And Michael Douglas.

00:09:45.567 --> 00:09:47.267
-And Michael Douglas, too.
The whole cast is --

00:09:47.267 --> 00:09:48.801
-And Kathryn Newton,
who was here.

00:09:48.801 --> 00:09:50.801
-By the way, she hit a home run
in this movie.

00:09:50.801 --> 00:09:52.367
She's phenomenal.
-How great is she?

00:09:52.367 --> 00:09:53.367
-Everyone's going to fall
in love with her.

00:09:53.367 --> 00:09:54.801
-Yeah. She's awesome.

00:09:54.801 --> 00:09:59.100
-It's really good that you get
sent into the quantum realm

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.067
through this thing
that your daughter invents.

00:10:01.067 --> 00:10:03.334
It's like a beacon that she
shouldn't have sent out.

00:10:03.334 --> 00:10:04.534
And then you -- I don't want

00:10:04.534 --> 00:10:06.067
to explain what really --
-I think you just did.

00:10:06.067 --> 00:10:07.534
-Yeah, I did.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:07.534 --> 00:10:09.667
And then you got to --
-Marvel will be thrilled.

00:10:09.667 --> 00:10:12.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:12.601 --> 00:10:14.000
-I want to show --
-They don't really care, though.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.334
They're, like,
"Tell whatever you want."

00:10:15.334 --> 00:10:16.934
They don't mind. It's so weird.
Marvel doesn't care

00:10:16.934 --> 00:10:18.367
what you say, yeah.
-They love it.
They really love it, yeah.

00:10:18.367 --> 00:10:20.334
[ Laughter ]
Sorry, Marvel. It's really good.

00:10:20.334 --> 00:10:22.033
I want to show a clip.
Here's Paul Rudd

00:10:22.033 --> 00:10:24.767
in "Ant-Man and the Wasp:
Quantumania."

00:10:24.767 --> 00:10:25.467
Take a look at this.

00:10:25.467 --> 00:10:27.601
[ Cheering ]

00:10:27.601 --> 00:10:29.534
-"Do I miss the action?

00:10:29.534 --> 00:10:31.534
Sometimes.

00:10:31.534 --> 00:10:33.767
Will I be there
when the Avengers need me?

00:10:33.767 --> 00:10:35.100
Absolutely.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.300
I'd never turn my back on them.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:42.000
But right now, the only job
I want is being a dad.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.267
I love you, Cassie.

00:10:44.267 --> 00:10:45.801
Thanks for being my hero.

00:10:47.501 --> 00:10:49.434
And I'm sorry
I missed some birthdays.

00:10:49.434 --> 00:10:50.934
[ Awws ]

00:10:50.934 --> 00:10:53.567
And, for the rest of you kids
out there,

00:10:53.567 --> 00:10:55.334
word of advice --

00:10:55.334 --> 00:10:57.100
look out for the little guy."

00:10:58.667 --> 00:10:59.367
-Yeah.

00:10:59.367 --> 00:11:02.501
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:02.501 --> 00:11:03.601
-You're at a book signing.

00:11:03.601 --> 00:11:04.868
-Yeah, yeah, I probably

00:11:04.868 --> 00:11:06.968
should've said that,
shouldn't I? I guess, yeah.

00:11:06.968 --> 00:11:08.901
Scott Lang wrote a book after,
to tell everybody

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:10.834
what's been going on with the,
you know,

00:11:10.834 --> 00:11:12.434
the events of "Endgame"
and everything.

00:11:12.434 --> 00:11:15.000
-The thing I like about you
and your character in this

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.667
is that you do play --
you're the first kind of,

00:11:17.667 --> 00:11:21.167
in my mind, a funny superhero
dad type of character,

00:11:21.167 --> 00:11:22.634
where you're just --
it's very --

00:11:22.634 --> 00:11:25.033
your scenes are so comedic
and funny

00:11:25.033 --> 00:11:26.868
and your dynamic
with your daughter.

00:11:26.868 --> 00:11:29.367
I don't want to, again, spoil,
but, you crush it, buddy.

00:11:29.367 --> 00:11:30.801
-Well, thank you,
Jimmy, thank you.
-You crush it.

00:11:30.801 --> 00:11:33.067
I want -- The movie's going
to be huge all over the world

00:11:33.067 --> 00:11:34.934
and I want to make sure
that everyone,

00:11:34.934 --> 00:11:37.400
all audiences everywhere,
get to hear you talk about it.

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.701
So, if you don't mind,

00:11:38.701 --> 00:11:40.300
I'm going to do a new thing,
a new technology.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.334
It's called live dubbing, okay?
-Yeah.

00:11:42.334 --> 00:11:43.968
[ Laughter ]
-And we've never done this,
right on the show.

00:11:43.968 --> 00:11:45.767
I have this remote here, okay?

00:11:45.767 --> 00:11:49.567
And it will switch languages
every time I hit a button.

00:11:49.567 --> 00:11:51.601
[ Laughter ]
-Wow. Oh, alright.
-So, you want to try it?

00:11:51.601 --> 00:11:54.767
-Yeah.
-Here to talk about the new
movie "Ant-Man" is Paul Rudd.

00:11:54.767 --> 00:11:56.767
Tell us about "Ant-Man."

00:11:56.767 --> 00:11:59.067
-Alright. Well, sure.
You know,

00:11:59.067 --> 00:12:04.434
in "Quantumania,"
I play Scott Lang, aka Ant-Man,

00:12:04.434 --> 00:12:07.834
and, you know, my family are...

00:12:07.834 --> 00:12:09.901
[ Laughter ]

00:12:17.167 --> 00:12:18.400
[ Laughter ]

00:12:20.868 --> 00:12:22.834
[ Laughter ]

00:12:26.167 --> 00:12:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:12:28.167 --> 00:12:30.067
-Straight bussin', no cap.

00:12:30.067 --> 00:12:31.667
[ Laughter and applause ]
"Ant-Man" is low-key GOATed

00:12:31.667 --> 00:12:33.100
